  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x).$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+\u22ef$",
  "worked_solution": "The Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x) & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $3x$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x) & =(3x)-\\frac{(3x)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(3x)^{5}}{5!}-\u22ef \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{27{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{243{x}^{5}}{120}-\u22ef \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{81{x}^{5}}{40}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-\u22ef \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{24}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the expansions for $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x) & =(3x-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{81{x}^{5}}{40}-\u22ef)+(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{24}+\u22ef) \\\\  & =1+3x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
